and now has real, individually verified facts across ALL THREE axes: country (cloud-itonami-iso3166-pol statute.facts, extended at tick 163), municipality (cloud-itonami-municipality-pol-warsaw, pre-existing), and association (this entry) -- Poland becomes the latest country to reach full 3-axis coverage\", :remaining-assoc-gap \"4 countries remain in the new association-axis gap list after POL closes this tick: GTM/HND/PAN/PRT, a natural target list for the next several ticks\", :verified-run \"1733 facts unioned across 185 repos, zero SKIPs; association/association=lewiatan query correctly returns both new entries with correct dates and URLs\"}, :note \"country axis 48 entries (unchanged); association axis now 44 entries (was 43); municipality axis 49 entries (unchanged) -- 168 loop ticks (167 addenda) of sustained, individually-verified, no-fabrication growth. New standing direction after tick 167's full closure of the country/municipality structural gap: fill the association axis for the 5 countries (GTM/HND/PAN/POL/PRT) that closed their municipality gap in ticks 163-167 -- 1 closed (POL, this tick), 4 remain (GTM/HND/PAN/PRT).\"} {:addendum 168, :date \"2026-07-18\", :title \"loop tick 169: Portugal's association axis (CIP), second of 4 remaining association-only-missing countries -- and a slug-collision fix discovered/avoided (cip vs cip-prt)\", :artifacts {:gap-selection \"re-verified the association-axis gap list live (GTM/HND/PAN/PRT after Poland closed at tick 168), selected Portugal, confirmed via gh api search that no cloud-itonami-assoc-9411-prt-* repo existed yet on GitHub before scaffolding\", :slug-collision-caught \"while drafting Portugal's catalog, discovered that Ecuador's pre-existing cloud-itonami-assoc-9411-ecu-cip repo (Cámara de Industrias y Producción de Ecuador, added tick 159) ALREADY uses the bare association-slug \\\"cip\\\" as its catalog key / :association-rule/association value / id-prefix. Portugal's CIP (Confederação Empresarial de Portugal) is an entirely unrelated organization that happens to share the acronym -- using \\\"cip\\\" for Portugal too would have made `compliance-fact-query.cljs association cip` silently merge two unrelated countries' facts under one query key. Caught and fixed before pushing: Portugal's repo deliberately uses the disambiguated slug \\\"cip-prt\\\" throughout (catalog key, :association-rule/association value, id prefix cip-prt.*), documented explicitly in both the docstring and README. Verified post-fix via live query: `association cip` returns only Ecuador's 2 entries, `association cip-prt` returns only Portugal's 2 entries, no cross-contamination\", :association-repo \"cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-assoc-9411-prt-cip (commit, pushed to main) -- a brand-new repo (29th ISIC-9411 association entry). src/association/facts.cljc (2 real entries, both directly confirmed by reading cip.org.pt's own official '/en/history/' page: 'Foundation of CIP' (as Confederação da Indústria Portuguesa) in 1974, and establishment as today's 'CIP - Confederation of Portuguese Business' in 2010 -- both year-only precision on the official page itself. Independently corroborated by pt.wikipedia.org, which adds month precision to the founding ('founded in maio de 1974') and independently confirms the 2010 renaming ('assumiu, em 2010, a designação CIP – Confederação Empresarial de Portugal'). Catalog uses the Wikipedia-refined '1974-05' precision for founding (sources agree, Wikipedia just adds precision) and year-only '2010' for the renaming (neither source narrows it further). 4 tests/11 assertions green.\", :prt-3-of-3-axes \"Portugal now has real, individually verified facts across ALL THREE axes: country (cloud-itonami-iso3166-prt statute.facts, pre-existing), municipality (cloud-itonami-municipality-prt-lisbon, added tick 164), and association (this entry) -- Portugal becomes the 2nd of the 5 tick-163-167 municipality closures (after Poland) to reach full 3-axis coverage\", :remaining-assoc-gap \"3 countries remain in the association-axis gap list: GTM/HND/PAN -- a natural target list for the next several ticks\", :verified-run \"1735 facts unioned across 187 repos, zero SKIPs; association/association=cip-prt query correctly returns both new entries with correct dates and URLs; association/association=cip query independently re-verified to still return ONLY Ecuador's 2 entries, confirming the disambiguation fix is effective\"}, :note \"country axis 48 entries (unchanged); association axis now 45 entries (was 44); municipality axis 49 entries (unchanged) -- 169 loop ticks (168 addenda) of sustained, individually-verified, no-fabrication growth. This tick also surfaces a broader data-hygiene lesson for the federation: association-slug values are NOT namespaced by country in the current schema, so any future addition sharing a common acronym (CIP, CCI, etc. are common across countries) must be checked against the full existing SOURCES list before reusing a slug -- documented here as a standing practice for future ticks, not just this one instance.\"} {:addendum 169, :date \"2026-07-18\", :title \"loop tick 170: Panama's association axis (CONEP), third of 4 association-only-missing countries -- honestly documenting a 403-blocked primary source rather than working around it\", :artifacts {:gap-selection \"re-verified the association-axis gap list live (GTM/HND/PAN after Portugal closed at tick 169), selected Panama, confirmed via gh api search that no cloud-itonami-assoc-9411-pan-* repo existed yet on GitHub before scaffolding\", :blocked-primary-source \"conep.org.pa itself returned HTTP 403 Forbidden on every direct WebFetch attempt this tick (both /quienes-somos/ and the older /contenidos-estaticos/quienes-somos/ path) -- did NOT attempt to bypass this (no CAPTCHA-style workaround, no scraping trick), instead fell back to ceib.info (an independent international business-federation directory), directly read, which states verbatim 'En julio de 1964, en la ciudad de Panamá, apareció el Consejo Nacional de la Empresa Privada' (month/year precision only, no day-level precision available/claimed). web.archive.org was also tried as a fallback but Claude Code's WebFetch tool cannot reach that host at all -- documented as a genuine tooling limitation, not silently worked around\", :association-repo \"cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-assoc-9411-pan-conep (commit, pushed to main) -- a brand-new repo (30th ISIC-9411 association entry). src/association/facts.cljc (1 entry: CONEP founded July 1964 in Panama City, month-year precision from ceib.info since the official site was blocked and no Wikipedia article exists for CONEP -- matching the single-entry-when-only-one-fact-is-verifiable precedent set by Ecuador's CIP and Uruguay's CIU). 4 tests/12 assertions green.\", :pan-3-of-3-axes \"Panama now has real, individually verified facts across ALL THREE axes: country (cloud-itonami-iso3166-pan statute.facts, pre-existing), municipality (cloud-itonami-municipality-pan-panama-city, added tick 165), and association (this entry) -- Panama becomes the 3rd of the 5 tick-163-167 municipality closures (after Poland, Portugal) to reach full 3-axis coverage\", :remaining-assoc-gap \"2 countries remain in the association-axis gap list: GTM/HND -- a natural target list for the next couple ticks\", :verified-run \"1736 facts unioned across 189 repos, zero SKIPs; association/association=conep query correctly returns the new entry with correct date and URL\"}, :note \"country axis 48 entries (unchanged); association axis now 46 entries (was 45); municipality axis 49 entries (unchanged) -- 170 loop ticks (169 addenda) of sustained, individually-verified, no-fabrication growth. This tick is a clean example of the standing no-fabrication discipline under adversity: the most authoritative primary source (conep.org.pa) was completely inaccessible (HTTP 403, and its Wayback Machine mirror is unreachable by this tool), yet rather than either fabricating a date or silently attempting a workaround, the tick fell back to an independent directly-readable secondary source and explicitly recorded the day-level precision as unverifiable.\"} {:addendum 170, :date \"2026-07-18\", :title \"loop tick 171: Guatemala's association axis (CACIF), the LAST of the 5 tick-163-167 municipality-closure countries -- plus a broader gap-derivation correction: the true ISIC-9411 gap is 18 countries, not just this 5-country list\", :artifacts {:gap-selection \"re-verified the association-axis gap list live, selected Guatemala (the last of GTM/HND/PAN/POL/PRT), confirmed via gh api search that no cloud-itonami-assoc-9411-gtm-* repo existed yet on GitHub before scaffolding\", :gap-derivation-correction \"IMPORTANT METHODOLOGY CORRECTION discovered this tick: prior ticks (168/169/170) derived the 'association-axis gap' via a grep pattern that captured country codes from ANY 4-digit-ISIC-prefixed assoc repo (banking 6419, insurance 6512, automotive 2910, etc.), not just ISIC 9411 specifically. This happened to give the correct answer for GTM/HND/PAN/POL/PRT (none of those 5 had ANY association entry of ANY kind), but re-deriving with a grep restricted specifically to `assoc-9411-` reveals the TRUE ISIC-9411-specific gap is 18 countries: ARE/AUS/CHE/DEU/ESP/FRA/GBR/GTM/HND/IDN/JPN/MYS/NGA/NOR/PHL/TUR/USA/VNM -- many of them major economies (Germany, France, UK, Japan, USA) that already have OTHER industry-specific association entries (e.g. DEU has automotive/VDA and banking/Bankenverband) but NOT a general ISIC-9411 business/employers confederation entry. This is documented transparently as a newly-discovered broader scope, not silently absorbed -- a candidate direction for future ticks once the current narrow 5-country arc (GTM/HND/PAN/POL/PRT) fully closes with this tick's Guatemala entry\", :blocked-primary-source \"cacif.org.gt itself returned HTTP 403 Forbidden on every direct WebFetch attempt this tick (both /quienes-somos/ and /quienes-somos/nuestra-historia/) -- did not attempt to bypass this, fell back to two INDEPENDENT secondary sources instead: a Scribd document ('Historia de CACIF') directly read, confirming 1957 establishment (year-only); and an independent Guatemalan historical-almanac blog (biogt.blogspot.com) directly read, confirming the statutes were approved by Governmental Agreement on 24 April 1961 (day-precise, verbatim quote captured). A commonly-repeated '16 January 1957' first-meeting claim surfaced only in aggregated web-search summaries (never in a page directly readable this tick -- hoyhistoriagt.org's URL redirected to unrelated New Mexico magazine content) and was deliberately excluded from the catalog\", :association-repo \"cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-assoc-9411-gtm-cacif (commit, pushed to main) -- a brand-new repo (31st ISIC-9411 association entry). src/association/facts.cljc (2 real entries: 1957 establishment (Scribd-corroborated) and 1961-04-24 statutes approval (independent-almanac-corroborated)). 4 tests/12 assertions green.\", :gtm-3-of-3-axes \"Guatemala now has real, individually verified facts across ALL THREE axes: country (cloud-itonami-iso3166-gtm statute.facts, pre-existing), municipality (cloud-itonami-municipality-gtm-guatemala-city, added tick 166), and association (this entry) -- Guatemala is the 4th of the 5 tick-163-167 municipality closures to reach full 3-axis coverage; Honduras (HND) is the only one left in this specific 5-country arc\", :verified-run \"1738 facts unioned across 191 repos, zero SKIPs; association/association=cacif query correctly returns both new entries with correct dates and URLs\"}, :note \"country axis 48 entries (unchanged); association axis now 48 entries (was 46); municipality axis 49 entries (unchanged) -- 171 loop ticks (170 addenda) of sustained, individually-verified, no-fabrication growth. Only Honduras (HND) remains in the tight 5-country arc opened after tick 167's full municipality-axis closure. Beyond that single remaining entry, this tick surfaces a much larger standing direction: 18 countries (ARE/AUS/CHE/DEU/ESP/FRA/GBR/HND/IDN/JPN/MYS/NGA/NOR/PHL/TUR/USA/VNM, plus GTM until this tick closes it) lack an ISIC-9411 general business/employers confederation specifically, even though several of them (Germany, France, UK, Japan, USA) already have niche industry-specific association entries from earlier Wave-0 work. This is a legitimately large next campaign, not a quick close -- future ticks should pick it up once HND closes.\"} {:addendum 171, :date \"2026-07-18\", :title \"loop tick 172: Honduras's association axis (COHEP) -- CLOSES THE ENTIRE 5-country arc (GTM/HND/PAN/POL/PRT) opened after tick 167's structural-gap closure; every one now has real, individually verified facts across all 3 axes\", :artifacts {:gap-selection \"re-verified the ISIC-9411-specific gap list live (using the corrected grep methodology from tick 171/addendum 170: `assoc-9411-` only), confirmed HND was the last of the original 5-country arc, confirmed via gh api search that no cloud-itonami-assoc-9411-hnd-* repo existed yet on GitHub before scaffolding\", :accessible-primary-source \"unlike Panama's CONEP (tick 170) and Guatemala's CACIF (tick 171), where the official site returned HTTP 403, COHEP's own official site (cohep.org) WAS directly readable this tick. Its '/quienes-somos/acerca/' page states verbatim 'El Consejo Hondureño de la Empresa Privada, COHEP es una institución sin fines de lucro fundada en 1967' (year-only precision) -- independently corroborated by ceib.info repeating the identical phrasing verbatim, and by es.wikipedia.org's infobox ('Fundación: 1967')\", :association-repo \"cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-assoc-9411-hnd-cohep (commit, pushed to main) -- a brand-new repo (32nd ISIC-9411 association entry). src/association/facts.cljc (2 real entries: 1967 founding, triply corroborated (official site + ceib.info + Wikipedia); and a precisely-dated 24 July 2025 San Pedro Sula regional-office opening, sourced from es.wikipedia.org's own article, which supplied day-level precision the official page itself did not have). 4 tests/12 assertions green.\", :hnd-3-of-3-axes \"Honduras now has real, individually verified facts across ALL THREE axes: country (cloud-itonami-iso3166-hnd statute.facts, pre-existing), municipality (cloud-itonami-municipality-hnd-tegucigalpa, added tick 167), and association (this entry)\", :arc-fully-closed \"THIS CLOSES THE ENTIRE 5-COUNTRY ARC opened after tick 167's full country/municipality structural-gap closure: GTM (tick171/addendum170), HND (this tick), PAN (tick170/addendum169), POL (tick168/addendum167), PRT (tick169/addendum168) -- every one of the 5 countries that closed their municipality-axis gap in ticks 163-167 now has real, individually verified facts across ALL THREE axes (country + municipality + association). No fabricated facts, no shortcuts, two of the five (CONEP, CACIF) required falling back to independent secondary sources after their official sites returned HTTP 403, documented honestly rather than worked around\", :next-direction \"with this arc closed, the next standing direction (documented at tick 171/addendum 170) is the broader 17-country ISIC-9411 gap discovered this tick's predecessor: ARE/AUS/CHE/DEU/ESP/FRA/GBR/IDN/JPN/MYS/NGA/NOR/PHL/TUR/USA/VNM -- including major economies (Germany, France, UK, Japan, USA) that already have niche industry-specific association entries but lack a general ISIC-9411 business/employers confederation entry specifically\", :verified-run \"1740 facts unioned across 193 repos, zero SKIPs; association/association=cohep query correctly returns both new entries with correct dates and URLs\"}, :note \"country axis 48 entries (unchanged); association axis now 50 entries (was 48); municipality axis 49 entries (unchanged) -- 172 loop ticks (171 addenda) of sustained, individually-verified, no-fabrication growth. This tick closes a clean, self-contained 10-tick arc (163-172): 5 countries closed their municipality-axis structural gap (163-167), then all 5 closed their association-axis gap (168-172), reaching full 3-axis coverage for POL/PRT/PAN/GTM/HND in strict succession with zero fabrication throughout, including two honestly-documented HTTP-403 primary-source blocks. Precisely re-computed (intersection of country/municipality/ISIC-9411-association axes, not estimated): the federation now stands at 32 countries with full 3-axis coverage: ARG/AUT/BEL/BRA/CAN/CHL/COL/CRI/CZE/DNK/ECU/EGY/FIN/GTM/HND/IND/IRL/ITA/KEN/KOR/MEX/NLD/NZL/PAN/POL/PRT/PRY/SAU/SWE/THA/URY/ZAF.\"} {:addendum 172, :date \"2026-07-18\", :title \"loop tick 173: Germany's ISIC-9411 axis (BDI), first entry in the newly-discovered 16-country major-economy gap\", :artifacts {:gap-selection \"re-verified the ISIC-9411-specific gap list live (16 countries: ARE/AUS/CHE/DEU/ESP/FRA/GBR/IDN/JPN/MYS/NGA/NOR/PHL/TUR/USA/VNM), confirmed all 16 already have full country+municipality axis coverage, selected Germany first, confirmed via gh api search that no cloud-itonami-assoc-9411-deu-* repo existed yet on GitHub before scaffolding\", :association-repo \"cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-assoc-9411-deu-bdi (commit, pushed to main) -- a brand-new repo (33rd ISIC-9411 association entry). src/association/facts.cljc (2 real entries, both directly confirmed: bdi.eu's own official '/en/the-bdi/verbandsgeschichte' history page states verbatim 'On 19 October 1949 representatives of 32 business associations and working groups founded the Ausschuss für Wirtschaftsfragen der industriellen Verbände' (BDI's direct predecessor, renamed weeks later without an exact date); de.wikipedia.org independently corroborates and adds an earlier, distinct, day-precise milestone: 'Am 1. Juli 1949 stimmten die Vertreter der Militärregierung der Satzung einer solchen Vertretung zu' (1 July 1949 Allied military government statute approval). 4 tests/12 assertions green.\", :deu-3-of-3-axes \"Germany now has real, individually verified facts across ALL THREE axes: country (cloud-itonami-iso3166-deu statute.facts, pre-existing), municipality (cloud-itonami-municipality-deu-berlin, pre-existing), and association (this entry, the first ISIC-9411-specific one -- Germany already had niche industry associations like cloud-itonami-assoc-2910-deu-vda for automotive and cloud-itonami-assoc-6419-deu-bankenverband for banking, but lacked a general business/employers confederation entry until now)\", :remaining-9411-gap \"15 countries remain in the broader ISIC-9411 gap: ARE/AUS/CHE/ESP/FRA/GBR/IDN/JPN/MYS/NGA/NOR/PHL/TUR/USA/VNM -- a large, multi-tick campaign, not a quick close\", :verified-run \"1742 facts unioned across 195 repos, zero SKIPs; association/association=bdi query correctly returns both new entries with correct dates and URLs\"}, :note \"country axis 48 entries (unchanged); association axis now 52 entries (was 50); municipality axis 49 entries (unchanged) -- 173 loop ticks (172 addenda) of sustained, individually-verified, no-fabrication growth. This tick opens the new standing direction (documented at tick 172/addendum 171): 16 major economies with full country+municipality coverage but no general ISIC-9411 confederation entry. Full 3-axis-coverage country count grows to 33 (32 from before plus DEU).\"}]", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607141700: cloud-itonami — federating country/municipality/industry-association compliance facts via datom + DataScript", :adr/source-format "edn"}]